# Doom-64-DC-X: nothing taken from the game, or from the Dreamcast port's data,
# is ever committed. You supply the ROM; setup.py makes the rest locally.

# --- your game files -------------------------------------------------------
# N64 ROMs in any byte order, and the Nightdive IWAD (optional Lost Levels)
*.z64
*.v64
*.n64
*.u64
*.rom
*.wad
*.WAD

# --- fetched and generated by setup.py ------------------------------------
# the Dreamcast port at its pinned revision, for its data (music, sound
# effects, normal maps, the Knee-Deep levels): fetched, never committed
/extern/
# wadtool and what it extracts from the ROM
/build/
# the disc's data folder: ROM-derived WADs and the fetched audio
/data/
# the dashboard icons (made from the fetched cover art)
/Platform/xbox/gen/
# game data in any other place it might be dropped
*.adpcm
*.tex
*.cmp
*.lmp
*.dt
selfboot/

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
/out/
# Visual Studio's build: its output, and its intermediates under the project name
/Xbox/
/Doom-64-DC-X/
*.iso
*.xbe
*.exe
*.obj
*.o
*.pdb
*.lib
*.cdi
*.elf

# --- tools -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.vs/
*.vcxproj.user
.vscode/
.claude/
*.log
